  "1381 A1B1 · Fold Tilt": "A narrow pulse shifted inside its cycle against random atoms that glitter, slightly detuned; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, LFO 3 tilts the scales from dark to bright, LFO 2 drifts the wavelet towards Daubechies 20, and each note opens its scale filter on its own envelope.",
  "1382 A1B1 · Mirage & Wire": "A Haar saw read from the middle of its cycle against scales that die from the top, like a pluck; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Daubechies 20, by an amount the LFO swings, LFO 3 changes how much of the upper scales survives the decay, and LFO 2 pulls the even scales in and out.",
  "1383 A1A2 · Weave Mallets": "A nasal pulse against a veil of band-passed noise; the scale cutoff breathes, the wavelet morphs towards Haar, LFO 2 pulls the source wave between narrow and wide, LFO 3 widens and narrows the filtered window, and a 24 dB OTA low-pass (2554 Hz) that opens on every note.",
  "1384 A1A2 · Sweep of Nasal": "A nasal pulse against a tick of noise; each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Daubechies 20, by an amount the LFO swings, the filtered part of the cycle is swept along it, LFO 2 thins and thickens the atoms (sparsity), LFO 3 changes how far each note's envelope opens the scale filter, and a 24 dB OTA low-pass (2859 Hz).",
  "1385 A1A2B1 · Stair Edge": "A nasal pulse against a veil of band-passed noise two octaves above, and stepped Walsh atoms, slightly detuned; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, the filtered part of the cycle is swept along it, LFO 3 sharpens and relaxes the edge of the scale filter, and LFO 2 widens and narrows the filtered window.",
  "1386 A1B1 · Strum & Velvet": "A warm saw against scales that die from the top, like a pluck; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Daubechies 2, by an amount the LFO swings, LFO 2 pulls the even scales in and out, LFO 3 sharpens and relaxes the edge of the scale filter, and a 24 dB ladder low-pass (1449 Hz) that opens on every note with some bite.",
  "1387 A1B1 · Choir Shift Piano": "Wavelet drawbars like an organ against a saw whose filter works in one part of the cycle an octave above; the wavelet morphs towards Haar, the scale cutoff breathes, LFO 2 slides the source inside its cycle, so the atoms meet other parts of the wave (source phase), and LFO 3 tilts the scales from dark to bright.",
  "1388 A1A2B1 · Air Mallets": "A nasal pulse against a woody knock an octave above, and a halo of high random atoms two octaves above; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, the filtered part of the cycle is swept along it, LFO 3 pulls the even scales in and out, LFO 2 sweeps the scale filter, and a 24 dB OTA low-pass (1630 Hz) that opens on every note.",
  "1389 A1A2B1 · Pixel Atoms Pluck": "Ramp atoms that open like a horn against a gritty Haar saw, slightly detuned, and a veil of band-passed noise two octaves above; the wavelet morphs towards Daubechies 20, LFO 3 thins and thickens the atoms (sparsity), LFO 2 carries the window of the scale filter round the cycle, and a 24 dB ladder low-pass (2023 Hz) that opens on every note with some bite.",
  "1390 A1B1 · Glint Strum": "A warm saw against random atoms that glitter a fifth above; the sparsity swings between a rich tone and a few wavelet atoms, each note's envelope pushes the wavelet towards Daubechies 20, by an amount the LFO swings, LFO 2 swells the resonance, and LFO 3 sweeps the scale filter.",
